  "created": "2022-08-16T12:20:39.451Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As it stands, the current Quick Menu settings is rather encumbered with options. However, with UI 2.0 a ways off, and the Quick Menu **preferably containing most of these options anyways**, a **simple** means of organization is in order.\nSuggestion is to use a \"segmented control\" — similar to that used for avatar visibility on profiles — to paginate the settings panel.\nSettings relating to safety and performance (Avatar Hiding, Debug/Developer options) would be placed in a Safety page, whereas settings relating to accessibility (Moveable Menu, Horizon Adjust, Near-clip, etc.) would be placed in an Accessibility page. All remaining options would be sorted under \"General\".\nAttached is a mockup demonstrating the appearance of a segmented pagination system.",
